From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <engine@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:04:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] page: Fire Emblem Fates picker: show Seal of Flames only when
 it is added

Round 83, the Seal edition split, round A step A1 (docs/SEAL_EDITION_PLAN.md
sections 3 and 7, H1-H5; the owner's request for an optional Seal of Flames
edition and his "Yes, that order" to Grok's order in
docs/collab/SEAL_EDITION_SPLIT_GROK.md; call 1 taken by default, F-070).
Grok's rule was an engine build only if the page cannot already hide Seal
of Flames. It could not: the Choose your game page opened at every windowed
start of a Fire Emblem Fates program, with Seal of Flames greyed and an
Install button, and Esc > Switch game was always set. Seal of Flames is
Laz14's fan mod (gamebanana.com/mods/656034, CC BY-NC-ND 4.0); no byte of
it is read or shipped, and "installed" is still decided from folder names
and the profile's own JSON.

A runtime check keyed on SealStatus, one program for both editions, no
cargo feature, no file moves:

- H1 (game_pick::page_wanted, windowed_start): the page opens only when
  picker_applies() and Seal of Flames is Installed or Broken (a broken
  install still gets its repair line). Missing: Fire Emblem Fates starts at
  once (lib.rs: App::begin, the page's own start path, with nothing
  remembered, so the player's game-choice.txt stays as it is; a start that
  fails shows the page with why, as before).
- H2 (game_pick::switch_offer): apply_choice leaves menus.switch_game empty
  when the other game is a Seal of Flames that is Missing. Installed: as
  before; Broken: greyed with the reason, as before.
- H3: a remembered Seal choice, --game seal or FEF_GAME_CHOICE=seal with a
  window while Seal of Flames is Missing starts Fire Emblem Fates with one
  log line. Headless --game seal keeps its error exit, unchanged.
- H4 (game_pick::sof_script, port_folder): the port-folder finder and the
  Install button look for tools\seal\sof.py first, then tools\play\sof.py
  (the Seal edition's new home; the old place keeps working).
- H5: the headless report's first boot record (FEF_HEADLESS_REPORT) gains
  "page": "would open", "skipped (Seal not installed)" or "skipped (not a
  Fire Emblem Fates program)" (game_pick::page_line), so the hide is proved
  with no window. Headless runs still never open the page; the other
  record fields and every robot path are unchanged.

Tests (game_pick, no window): new
with_no_seal_of_flames_the_page_is_skipped_and_there_is_no_switch_game,
with_seal_of_flames_installed_the_page_opens_and_switch_game_is_offered,
with_seal_of_flames_broken_the_page_opens_for_the_repair,
a_remembered_or_asked_for_seal_of_flames_that_is_missing_starts_fates,
sof_py_is_found_in_tools_seal_first_then_tools_play; changed on purpose:
the_page_preselects_and_greys_seal_of_flames_when_it_cannot_be_chosen now
also says the page is not wanted while Seal is missing and is wanted once
it is installed. Eight planted bugs (page ignores Seal; page hides a broken
Seal; Switch game always offered; no log line; the remembered Seal started;
tools\play first; finder ignores tools\seal; report says "would open" when
skipped) each fail at least one test (build/r83/eng/planted.txt).
cargo test -p zakuro --lib: 136 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored (real-game
tests, as before).
